    "name": "Reverse SSH tunnel — AWS",
    "story": "When the Private Network Gateway is not an option and the corporate firewall blocks inbound traffic from the cloud, serverless compute can reach on-premises resources through a reverse SSH tunnel. A private endpoint rule in the workspace's NCC connects over AWS PrivateLink to a VPC endpoint service fronting a Network Load Balancer, whose targets are proxy EC2 instances. On-premises tunnel hosts run autossh and open outbound SSH connections to the proxies across the Transit Gateway and Direct Connect / Site-to-Site VPN; the proxies run socat and expose each on-premises resource's port. Serverless traffic flows NLB → proxy → tunnel → tunnel host → resource. The customer runs and maintains the proxies and tunnel hosts: at least two proxies, and a distinct port mapping on each proxy for each resource.",
